menu "CNC Tool Monitor V2"

    config SMU_USE_MOCK
        bool "Use software SMU mock instead of real I2C hardware"
        default y
        help
            When enabled, telemetry.c drives its two SMU links through
            smu_mock.c — a software stand-in that runs the real
            spindle_sm.c/alarm.c logic against a synthesized cutting
            cycle, including the two-phase config commit and fault
            injection (link drop, CRC corruption, frozen sequence
            numbers, sensor faults). No SMU hardware or I2C wiring is
            needed.

            When disabled, telemetry.c drives its links through
            smu_i2c_transport.c against real SMU hardware on the two I2C
            buses defined in board.h (SMU1_I2C_*/SMU2_I2C_*).

            Defaults to y because, as of the V2 migration that added this
            option, no SMU hardware exists yet to test against — see
            FIRMWARE_DESIGN_SPEC.md and the "accepted risks" section of
            the migration plan. Set to n once real SMUs are available.

endmenu
